{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n  Quicksort\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <limits.h>\\n#include <openssl/md5.h>\\n\\n#define QUICK_SORT_PARALLEL_MIN 16384\\n#define QUICK_SORT_TASK_CUTOFF 2048\\n\\n/*\\n * Prototypes\\n */\\nvoid srandnum(int seed);\\ndouble randnum(void);\\nint *generate_case(int N);\\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax);\\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j);\\nint partition(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N);\\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N);\\n\\n/*\\n * A generic pRNG\\n */\\n#define MY_RAND_MAX 0x7FFFFFFF\\n\\n#define RANDNUM_W 521288629\\n#define RANDNUM_Z 362436069\\n\\nunsigned int randum_w = RANDNUM_W;\\nunsigned int randum_z = RANDNUM_Z;\\n\\nvoid srandnum(int seed)\\n{\\n    unsigned int w, z;\\n    w = (seed * 104623) & 0xffffffff;\\n    randum_w = (w) ? w : RANDNUM_W;\\n    z = (seed * 48947) & 0xffffffff;\\n    randum_z = (z) ? z : RANDNUM_Z;\\n}\\n\\ndouble randnum(void)\\n{\\n    unsigned int u;\\n    randum_z = 36969 * (randum_z & 65535) + (randum_z >> 16);\\n    randum_w = 18000 * (randum_w & 65535) + (randum_w >> 16);\\n    u = (randum_z << 16) + randum_w;\\n    return (abs(u));\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Main function\\n */\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[])\\n{\\n    int N = 0;\\n    int *our_list = NULL;\\n\\n    //The input provides the case size\\n    scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &N);\\n    if (N <= 0) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error: please, provide the case size.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    //Generate the case\\n    our_list = generate_case(N);\\n    if (our_list == NULL) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error: case instantiation failed.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    //Do the thing\\n    quicksort(our_list, N);\\n\\n    if (is_sorted(our_list, N) == 1) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error, for some reason list is still unsorted.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n#ifdef COMPUTE_MD5_PROBLEM\\n    //Compute MD5 Checksum for problem identification\\n    MD5_CTX c;\\n    unsigned char out[MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH];\\n    MD5_Init(&c);\\n    MD5_Update(&c, our_list, N * sizeof(int));\\n    MD5_Final(out, &c);\\n    for (int n = 0; n < MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH; n++) {\\n        printf(\\\"%02x\\\", out[n]);\\n    }\\n#endif\\n    printf(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n\\n    //Clean up\\n    free(our_list);\\n\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Public API\\n */\\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N)\\n{\\n    if (N < QUICK_SORT_PARALLEL_MIN) {\\n        _quicksort(toorder, 0, N - 1);\\n        return;\\n    }\\n\\n    /* Recursive partitions have disjoint ranges after partitioning. */\\n    #pragma omp parallel\\n    {\\n        #pragma omp single\\n        _quicksort(toorder, 0, N - 1);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Internal recursive function to quicksort\\n */\\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\\n{\\n    if (lo >= hi)\\n        return;\\n\\n    int b = partition(toorder, lo, hi);\\n    int left_count = b - lo;\\n    int right_count = hi - b;\\n\\n    /* Keep the dependent partition loop serial; sort independent ranges as tasks. */\\n    if (left_count >= right_count && left_count > QUICK_SORT_TASK_CUTOFF) {\\n        int task_lo = lo;\\n        int task_hi = b - 1;\\n        #pragma omp task firstprivate(toorder, task_lo, task_hi)\\n        _quicksort(toorder, task_lo, task_hi);\\n        _quicksort(toorder, b + 1, hi);\\n        #pragma omp taskwait\\n    } else if (right_count > QUICK_SORT_TASK_CUTOFF) {\\n        int task_lo = b + 1;\\n        int task_hi = hi;\\n        #pragma omp task firstprivate(toorder, task_lo, task_hi)\\n        _quicksort(toorder, task_lo, task_hi);\\n        _quicksort(toorder, lo, b - 1);\\n        #pragma omp taskwait\\n    } else {\\n        _quicksort(toorder, lo, b - 1);\\n        _quicksort(toorder, b + 1, hi);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Swap two values.\\n */\\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j)\\n{\\n    int temp = toorder[i];\\n    toorder[i] = toorder[j];\\n    toorder[j] = temp;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Partition decision\\n */\\nint partition(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\\n{\\n    int b = lo;\\n    int r;\\n\\n    /* randnum updates shared state, so protect pivot draws across tasks. */\\n    #pragma omp critical(quicksort_rng_lock)\\n    {\\n        r = (int) (lo + (hi - lo) * (randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX));\\n    }\\n\\n    int pivot = toorder[r];\\n    swap(toorder, r, hi);\\n    for (int i = lo; i < hi; i++) {\\n        if (toorder[i] < pivot) {\\n            swap(toorder, i, b);\\n            b++;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    swap(toorder, hi, b);\\n    return b;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Check if elements are in non-decreasing order\\n */\\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N)\\n{\\n    int unsorted = 0;\\n\\n    #pragma omp simd reduction(|:unsorted)\\n    for (int i = 1; i < N; i++) {\\n        unsorted |= toorder[i] < toorder[i - 1];\\n    }\\n    return unsorted;\\n}\\n\\n\\n/*\\n * Generate a case\\n */\\nint *generate_case(int N)\\n{\\n    int i;\\n    int *ret = NULL;\\n\\n    // Make case generation reproducible\\n    srandnum(0);\\n\\n    // Allocate memory\\n    ret = (int *) malloc(N * sizeof(int));\\n    if (ret == NULL) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error: some malloc won't work.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return NULL;\\n    }\\n    // Get pseudo-random positive integer values\\n    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) {\\n        ret[i] = drand(0, INT_MAX);\\n    }\\n    return ret;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * A pseudo-random number between two positive integer values\\n */\\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax)\\n{\\n    return xmin + (xmax - xmin) * randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/quicksort.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"For sufficiently large arrays, OpenMP tasks on the disjoint recursive quicksort ranges can use the available CPU cores while retaining the serial partition loop whose boundary index has a loop-carried dependency. A task-size cutoff should limit scheduling overhead; serializing pivot RNG draws avoids races without changing the sorted result.\",\"notes\":\"Unmeasured candidate. OpenMP directives leave the recursive serial behavior intact when OpenMP is not enabled. The generator, checksum, output, and existing SIMD sortedness check are preserved.\",\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Run large top-level sorts in an OpenMP parallel/single region and task the larger independent recursive range, sorting the other range inline; use cutoffs to limit parallel-region and task overhead.\",\"Keep the partition scan serial because its boundary index is loop-carried, and protect shared RNG state while concurrent tasks select pivots.\",\"Preserve the existing SIMD reduction for the post-sort sortedness check and leave case generation and checksum behavior unchanged.\"]}"}}
